'''Laua''', also known as '''Labu''', is an extinct [[Mailuan languages|Mailuan language]] of [[Papua New Guinea]].  It was spoken in the [[Central Province (Papua New Guinea)|Central Province]], north and west of Laua according to ''[[Ethnologue]]''. Laua had only one remaining speaker in 1987, and became extinct shortly after.

